	"description": [
		"Students explore casting as a sculptural process across multiple material systems, including plaster, wax, paper pulp, reusable molds, and 3D-printed molds integrated with hands-on fabrication. The course emphasizes sustainable, low-energy materials and introduces digital fabrication as a tool for mold-making and form development. Through studio work, readings, and discussion, students build technical skill and conceptual grounding in contemporary casting practices. Materials fee. Offered annually in the spring semester. Open to majors and non-majors. Prerequisite: ARTS 103."
	],
